ent":"createToastManager"},"2626":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-20","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/toast#exports","content":"Exports"},"2627":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-21","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#usage","content":"Toast is built on Base UI's\nToast. The package\nexports a module-level singleton toastManager and a ToastProvider\nthat auto-mounts the viewport — drop <ToastProvider> once at the app\nroot and call toastManager.add(...) from anywhere (event handlers,\nfetch interceptors, zustand actions, …). No hook required at the call\nsite."},"2628":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-22","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#status","content":"type accepts success, warning, error, info, or loading.\nThe toast applies the matching colour but does not pick an icon —\nicons are opt-in via data.icon. The loading status swaps the\nclose X for a cancel button when data.cancelProps is supplied."},"2629":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-23","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#position","content":"ToastProvider accepts a position prop with six anchors:\ntop-left, top-center, top-right, bottom-left, bottom-center,\nbottom-right. One provider serves one position — toasts dispatched\nthrough its manager render at that anchor."},"2630":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-24","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#multiple-positions-two-channels","content":"To send some toasts to one corner and others to a different corner,\ncreate a second manager with createToastManager and nest a second\nToastProvider for it. Each provider/manager pair is a separate\nchannel — pick whichever you want at the call site."},"2631":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-25","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/compo