ces","content":"Surfaces"},"2899":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-11","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#actions","content":"Actions"},"2900":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-12","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#status","content":"Status"},"2901":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-13","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#form","content":"Form"},"2902":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-14","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#charts","content":"Charts"},"2903":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-15","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"Sidebar"},"2904":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-16","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#vittal-extensions","content":"Vittal Extensions"},"2905":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-17","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#avatar-palette","content":"Avatar Palette"},"2906":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-18","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#tag-palette","content":"Tag Palette"},"2907":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-19","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#overview","content":"Vittal Design follows the shadcn/ui\nnaming convention for its semantic layer. Colors are defined under\ntokens/ (Style Dictionary), built into src-v2/styles/tokens/generated.css\nas CSS custom properties on :root, and exposed to Tailwind via\n@theme inline (--color-*)."},"2908":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-20","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#overview","content":"Primitive scales (--primary-50…900, --grayscale-100…900,\n--grayscale-opacity-100…900, --success-100…900, etc.) — internal\nfoundation. Reach for these when you need a specific shade for\ncharts, illustrations, or fine-grained tinting. Tailwind utility:\nbg-primary-500, text-grayscale-700, etc."},"2909":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-21","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#overview","content":"Semantic tokens (--background, --primary, --card,\n--destructive, …) — the public API. These describe intent\nand pair with -foreground siblings for legible content on the\nsurface. Tailwind utility: bg-primary text-primary-foreground."},"2910":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-22","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#overview","content":"Component tokens (--avatar-*-fg, --tag-*-solid) — closed\npalettes used by specific components."},"2911":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-23","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#primary","content":"The primary palette is a blue scale used for interactive elements,\nbuttons, focus states, and key affordances."},"2912":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-24","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#grayscale","content":"The default grayscale palette is fully solid — use it whenever the\nsurface must be opaque (popovers, tooltips, toasts, solid chips)."},"2913":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-25","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#grayscale-opacity","content":"The opacity variant uses rgba(35, 35, 50, α) so it tonally adapts\nover any background. Use it for hover tints, dividers, disabled fields,\nand other states where translucency is desired. --grayscale-opacity-900\nis the only solid hex."},"2914":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-26","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#success","content":"Positive feedback, confirmations, \"saved\" states."},"2915":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-27","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#info","content":"Informational messaging and neutral status indicators."},"2916":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-28","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#warning","content":"Caution states — soft warnings that don't block flow."},"2917":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-29","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#destructive","content":"Errors, destructive actions, hard validation failures."},"2918":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-30","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#semantic-tokens","content":"Intent-based aliases that point to primitive colors. Each surface\nships with a paired -foreground token — use them together so text\nremains legible regardless of theme overrides."},"2919":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-31","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#surfaces","content":"Page chrome, cards, popovers, and muted/accent regions. background\nis the page; card and popover are elevated containers; muted\nand accent are subtle background tints (e.g. table stripes, hover\nstates)."},"2920":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-32","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#actions","content":"Brand action surfaces. primary is the dominant call-to-action;\nsecondary is the alternative button surface."},"2921":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-33","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#status","content":"Feedback colors paired with foreground for legible content."},"2922":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-34","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#form","content":"Borders, input strokes, and focus rings. border is the canonical\nsolid divider; input matches it by default but can be themed\nindependently; ring paints focus outlines."},"2923":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-35","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#charts","content":"Five-step palette for data visualization. Defaults rotate through\nprimary → success → warning → info → destructive so chart series\ninherit brand color regardless of theme overrides."},"2924":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-36","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"Application sidebar shell slots (shadcn-compatible). Used by the\nSidebar primitive utilities such as\nbg-sidebar, text-sidebar-foreground, and border-sidebar-border.\nProduct blocks may override individual slots (for example\n[--sidebar:transparent] on the cloud shell)."},"2925":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-37","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"Slot"},"2926":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-38","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"Default alias"},"2927":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-39","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"--sidebar"},"2928":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-40","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"grayscale.100"},"2929":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-41","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags