80":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-166","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#imports","content":"Replace package imports with local imports:"},"3381":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-167","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#imports","content":"Compound components use named exports:"},"3382":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-168","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#button","content":"Button no longer owns icons or loading state. Move icons and spinners into children, and mark them with data-icon=\"inline-start\" or data-icon=\"inline-end\"."},"3383":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-169","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#button","content":"Replace isLoading with an explicit disabled button plus Spinner.\nInstall @vital-design/spinner if your app needs the shared spinner."},"3384":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-170","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#button","content":"Icon-only buttons now use size variants instead of empty children or icon props:"},"3385":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-171","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#button","content":"Keep size=\"md\" or size=\"lg\" for buttons with labels. For filled label buttons, v1 keeps the v0 spacing contract: the icon side is 12px, and the non-icon side is 16px.\nIf you used earlier v1 draft size names, rename medium to md, large to lg, icon-medium to icon-md, and icon-large to icon-lg."},"3386":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-172","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#button","content":"The variant prop renamed filled to default. The new ghost variant is a transparent button with hover background — use it inside popovers, toolbars, and split-button menus (it backs the Popup Button pattern)."},"3387":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-173","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#button","content":"The theme enum keeps alarm (filled red) and dangerous (white surface with red text) as distinct intents — alarm is only available on variant=\"default\". The dangerous theme renders bordered at size=\"md\" and shadow-elevated at size=\"lg\", mirroring the Figma \"Outlined\" guideline."},"3388":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-174","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#text-input-value-changes","content":"Input is built on Base UI's input primitive. For controlled value\nupdates, prefer onValueChange; keep native onChange only when the\ncaller needs the DOM change event."},"3389":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-175","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#invalid-form-controls","content":"V1-only isError props are removed from v2 form controls. Use aria-invalid on the actual control instead."},"3390":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-176","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#invalid-form-controls","content":"When using Field, set invalid state on both the field wrapper and the control: Field data-invalid handles label/help text styling, while aria-invalid on the actual control handles control semantics and the visible border."},"3391":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-177","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#switch","content":"Switch now follows the Base UI callback name. Replace onChange with onCheckedChange; root props such as defaultChecked, name, value, disabled, and aria-invalid pass through."},"3392":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-178","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"Install @vital-design/label when a migrated screen has standalone text associated with a form control."},"3393":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-179","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"Use Label for visible field labels that point at Input, InputGroupInput, Textarea, or PasswordInput with htmlFor."},"3394":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-180","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"Do not hide low-level label composition inside primitives:"},"3395":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-181","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"Checkbox and RadioGroupItem are control primitives. Pair them with Label htmlFor at the callsite."},"3396":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-182","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"InputGroupAddon is presentational. Use Label htmlFor outside the group when the field has visible label text."},"3397":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-183","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"Current v2 label audit:"},"3398":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-184","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"Location"},"3399":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-185","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"Migrate to Label?"},"3400":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-186","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"Notes"},"3401":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-187","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"src-v2/components/label/Label.tsx"},"3402":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-188","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"No"},"3403":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-189","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"The primitive implementation"},"3404":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-190","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"src-v2/components/checkbox/Checkbox.tsx"},"3405":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-191","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"Yes"},"3406":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-192","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"Pair with Label htmlFor at callsites"},"3407":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-193","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"src-v2/components/radio-group/RadioGroup.tsx"},"3408":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-194","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"Yes"},"3409":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-195","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"Pair items with Label htmlFor at callsites"},"3410":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-196","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"src-v2/components/input/input-group/InputGroup.test.tsx"},"3411":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-197","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"No"},"3412":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-198","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"Test-only render override for addon semantics"},"3413":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-199","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"App/docs examples around Input, InputGroupInput, Textarea, PasswordInput"},"3414":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-200","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"Yes"},"3415":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-201","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"Add Label htmlFor when the field has visible label text"},"3416":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-202","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#styling","content":"v0 components depend on styled-components.\nv1 components use Tailwind CSS 4 utilities and Vittal Design CSS variables."},"3417":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-203","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#styling","content":"Do not import src-v2/styles/* from the npm package. Use the registry install so the theme is written to your app CSS."},"3418":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-204","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#lists","content":"ActionList and ActionInfiniteList are removed in v1. Pick the v1 replacement by intent:"},"3419":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-205","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#lists","content":"Action menu (each item fires a callback, no value binding) → DropdownMenu."},"3420":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-206","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#lists","content":"Searchable value picker → Combobox. Hierarchical → Command + Popover."},"3421":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-207","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#lists","content":"Display row or detail list → Item + ItemGroup. Use size=\"list\" for select-option density."},"3422":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-208","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#lists","content":"Searchable command panel (you own search, loading, paging, empty text) → Command."},"3423":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-209","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#treeselect","content":"Move TreeSelect screens to a Command + Popover recipe.\nThe old component owned more data behavior. In v1, the screen owns the path, search value, loading state, and child loading. See the Command Storybook HierarchicalPicker story for the recommended shape."},"3424":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-210","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#treeselect","content":"Use Combobox instead if the old screen only needed searchable flat options."},"3425":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-211","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#migration-checklist","content":"Install the v1 registry item."},"3426":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-212","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#migration-checklist","content":"Replace @fed/vital-design imports on the screen."},"3427":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-213","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#migration-checklist","content":"Update props to the v1 component API."},"3428":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-214","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#migration-checklist","content":"Add the Tailwind and theme setup once per app."},"3429":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-215","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#migration-checklist","content":"Test keyboard behavior for pickers, popups, and list rows."},"3430":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-216","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#migration-checklist","content":"Remove v0 dependencies after the last v0 import is gone."},"3431":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","type":"page","content":"Tailwind CSS Setup","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup"},"3432":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-0","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","content":"Configure Tailwind CSS 4 to work with Vittal Design components and design tokens."},"3433":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-1","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#overview","content":"Overview"},"3434":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-2","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#registry-installed-local-components","content":"Registry-Installed Local Components"},"3435":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-3","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#design-tokens","content":"Design Tokens"},"3436":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-4","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#postcss-configuration","content":"PostCSS Configuration"},"3437":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-5","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#fonts","content":"Fonts"},"3438":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-6","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#style-isolation-with-data-slot","content":"Style isolation with data-slot"},"3439":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-7","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#naming","content":"Naming"},"3440":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-8","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#scoping-styles-in-your-app","content":"Scoping styles in your app"},"3441":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-9","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#which-parts-get-a-slot","content":"Which parts get a slot?"},"3442":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-10","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#coverage-status","content":"Coverage status"},"3443":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-11","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#overview","content":"This page applies to registry-installed Vittal Design components. When you install src-v2/ components through the shadcn-compatible registry, the CLI copies them into your app and injects the Vittal Design theme tokens plus small base CSS rules into the CSS file configured in components.json."},"3444":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-12","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#overview","content":"If you are maintaining an existing project that still uses the published @fed/vital-design npm package, keep that legacy src/ integration as-is. The npm package does not expose the registry-only src-v2 stylesheet as a public import."}